.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.db
.superpowers/

# generated by scripts/make_sample_wav.py
*.wav
# ...except the committed demo audio, which a clean clone cannot regenerate:
# replay fixtures are named for the SHA256 of this exact PCM.
!samples/*.wav

# Build outputs of `make track` / `make bench` -- regenerable from committed
# audio and fixtures. results/scored.json is deliberately NOT here: it is
# measured calibration data that cost real money and hours to produce.
results/track.json
results/report.md

# Calibration run artifacts. Regenerable by `dhvani-calibrate collect`, and
# large: 150 segments of raw PCM is ~31 MB of .npy that nothing in the repo
# reads. results/scored.json is the CURATED, committed phase-1 output; a
# root-level scored.json is just the last run's output file (the CLI's
# default --scored-out) and is not the same thing.
calibration_pcm/
/scored.json
delta_table_tier2.json
